{"alignments":[],"candidates":[{"additionalConceptCount":0,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 194","reason":"Squaring a+a^-1 = 4 gives a^2+a^-2 = 16-2 = 14. Squaring again gives a^4+a^-4 = 14^2-2 = 194.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2007_AMC_10A_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"id":"square-reciprocal-sums","label":"Square reciprocal sums","nodeIds":["cnm_149"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_164","cnm_143"],"id":"solution:square-reciprocal-sums:741045191318","label":"Square the given sum twice","methodDirectNodeIds":{"square-reciprocal-sums":["cnm_149","cnm_148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_149","cnm_148","cnm_164","cnm_143"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 0","reason":"Since x is nonzero, squaring gives x^2+x^(-2)=3, and squaring again gives x^4+x^(-4)=7. Therefore x^11-7x^7+x^3=x^7(x^4-7+x^(-4))=0.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2021_AMC_10B_Q15","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"square-reciprocal-sums","label":"Use reciprocal powers","methodDirectNodeIds":{"square-reciprocal-sums":["cnm_149","cnm_148","cnm_162"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_149","cnm_148","cnm_162"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"factor-with-quartic-relation","label":"Factor with a known zero","methodDirectNodeIds":{"factor-with-quartic-relation":["cnm_149","cnm_148","cnm_151","cnm_152"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_149","cnm_148","cnm_151","cnm_152"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 9/4","reason":"The totals give a+b+c=13/4 and ab+bc+ca=11/4. Thus d^2=a^2+b^2+c^2=(13/4)^2-2(11/4)=81/16, so d=9/4. All body diagonals have this length; the volume is not needed.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2023_AMC_10B_Q17","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[